<title>USA: NJ Transit approves $105 mln project -- paper.</title>
<headline>NJ Transit approves $105 mln project -- paper.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Jersey Transit has approved a $105 million project to build a new concourse in New York City's Penn Station.</p>
<p>The new concourse is designed to reduce congestion to meet projections of a 50 percent increase in passenger traffic.</p>
<p>The New Jersey Transportation Trust Fund Authority and the Federal Transit Administration are providing the funding, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>Construction is expected to last until 2001.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
